            The fume cupboard is the most important protective device in the laboratory – and in the container it is at the same time the largest energy consumer and the most demanding ventilation node. This guide explains how a cupboard works, what DIN EN 14175 actually requires, which types exist and how extract and energy are solved cleanly in the container laboratory – with verified standards.
